.TH AXON-SERVER 1 "2026" "axon-server" "Axon"
.SH NAME
axon-server \- personal Matrix state layer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B axon-server
[\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Axon sits between a Matrix homeserver and clients.
It owns sync, E2EE decryption, search, and a media proxy,
and exposes a versioned HTTP + WebSocket API at /v1/.
.PP
With no command it runs the server.
.B axon-server init
writes a starter config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/axon-server/config.toml
Packaged-install config (generated on first configure when a local
Postgres cluster is reachable).
.TP
.I /var/lib/axon-server
Durable state (SDK store, search index, staged uploads).
.TP
.I /var/cache/axon-server
Disposable media cache.
.SH SEE ALSO
The source-tree
.I axon.toml.example
is the full config reference.
